From 3798787cc78a2dc91261afab3bad95cd0b7a3743 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:09:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): apply Syncthing-staged Rime profile from the app

Android blocks other apps from writing the app-private Rime data dir, so
Syncthing can only stage configs in Download/Rime-Sync/Rime-Arch. Add a
bridge that copies that folder into data/rime, drops librime's build/
cache, and restarts Fcitx so Rime redeploys:

* RimeProfileSync compares contents first and does nothing when the staged
  profile is unchanged, avoiding needless 2M-entry rebuilds.
* RimeImportReceiver (exported, READ_INPUT_STATE) allows adb/scripts to
  trigger the apply.
* Advanced settings gets 'Apply Syncthing Rime profile' plus en/zh strings.
* Release builds stay debuggable so run-as can inspect or recover the Rime
  dir when a deployment goes wrong.
